<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n24652" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">in-turbĭdus</span></b> , a, um,
			adj.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Pass.</i>, <i>undisturbed</i>, <i>quiet</i> (Tacitean): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">inturbidus externis rebus annus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tac. A.
					3, 52</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">juventa,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 14, 22</span></i>
			.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Act.</i>, <i>not turbulent</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vir sanctus, inturbidus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tac. H.
					3, 39</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
